Here is the commit message:
SOLR-11182: A split shard failure on IOException should be
 logged

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the failure to log split shard failures when an IOException occurred during the update process. This lack of logging meant that errors were not being properly tracked or reported, making it difficult to diagnose issues related to shard splitting.

Here is the patch:

   @Override
   public void split(SplitIndexCommand cmd) throws IOException {
     commit(new CommitUpdateCommand(cmd.req, false));
     SolrIndexSplitter splitter = new SolrIndexSplitter(cmd);
     splitCommands.mark();
     try {
       splitter.split();
     } catch (IOException e) {
       numErrors.increment();
       numErrorsCumulative.mark();
+      throw e;
     }
   }



