```
Reason:
The catch block for the IOException does not include any logging mechanism, which means that when an IOException occurs during the shard splitting process, the error is silently handled without any indication of failure. This lack of logging makes it difficult to diagnose issues related to shard splitting.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
catch (IOException e) {
  numErrors.increment();
  numErrorsCumulative.mark();
  throw e;
}
```
